      "visuals": [
        {
          "type": "textbox",
          "x": 16,
          "y": 56,
          "w": 616,
          "h": 300,
          "card": true,
          "alt": "What this report shows",
          "paragraphs": [
            {"text": "What this report shows", "size": 12, "bold": true},
            "A management P&L for Kaldora Facility Services, a facility-services company in Graz with four service lines (Cleaning Services, Technical Maintenance, Security Services, Catering) and two support departments (Administration, Sales & Marketing).",
            "Pages: the P&L statement with months, YTD and full year; the variance to budget by department and account group; the monthly trend; operating expenses; and the detail of one department (right-click a department bar, Drill through).",
            {"text": "Kaldora Facility Services is a fictional company and every number is invented.", "colour": "muted"},
            {"text": "Rebuilt from memory as a demo. The original client's name and data are not used.", "colour": "muted"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "textbox",
          "x": 648,
          "y": 56,
          "w": 616,
          "h": 300,
          "card": true,
          "alt": "Sign convention and definitions",
          "paragraphs": [
            {"text": "Sign convention and definitions", "size": 12, "bold": true},
            "The ledger export uses the ledger sign: debit plus, credit minus. The model stores every amount as its contribution to profit: income plus, expense minus. Revenue and cost lines show in display sign, so costs appear as positive amounts. A variance is favourable when it raises profit: more revenue or less cost.",
            "Closed months: the months up to the last actual month; the budget is compared with actuals only over them.",
            "Outlook: actuals up to the last closed month, the Q4 forecast after it. Full year adds the open months of the forecast.",
            "On plan: within 1 % of the budget, or within 0.1 percentage points on a margin line."
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "rows",
          "type": "tableEx",
          "x": 16,
          "y": 372,
          "w": 400,
          "h": 200,
          "title": "Rows per scenario",
          "roles": {"Values": [["DimScenario", "Scenario", "Column"], ["_Measures", "Rows", "Measure"]]},
          "sort": {"field": ["DimScenario", "Scenario", "Column"], "direction": "Ascending"}
        },
        {
          "type": "textbox",
          "x": 432,
          "y": 372,
          "w": 832,
          "h": 332,
          "card": true,
          "alt": "Data files, security and sources",
          "paragraphs": [
            {"text": "Data files, security and sources", "size": 12, "bold": true},
            "gl_actuals.csv: 3,178 ledger balances, January 2023 to September 2025. budget.xlsx: the sheets Budget 2023, Budget 2024, Budget 2025 and Forecast 2025, 98 rows each. chart_of_accounts.csv: 40 accounts. cost_centres.csv: 6 departments. pnl_layout.csv: the 10 P&L lines. security.csv: 10 rows.",
            "Row-level security: the Power BI project in the repository defines the role Department head, which limits a department head to the cost centres listed for their address; the copy made for Publish to web leaves the role out.",
            "Generated by tools/make_data.py with seed 43: uv run python tools/make_data.py",
            "Repository: github.com/HARISPAARTAN/financial-reporting-dashboard",
            "Replica: harispaartan.github.io/financial-reporting-dashboard"
          ]
        }
      ]
